format 1

# Seeded by `pklith seed --init` from the fragments this repository's
# files switch on (`pklith detect`). It is yours now: pklith never rewrites it.
#
# itok leaves the `*` row: `.context-limits` holds sherd's per-chain
# ceilings (paradigm/V12, root T4); itok reads the same file as per-file
# ceilings with another tokenizer, so the two disagree on every row, as
# nix-codebuff and nix-orca found. sherd-budget gates the ceilings.

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
# The registry judges itself, as in pklith, actlith and lablith: generated
# steps match .pklith, and every tracked file type has a row.
gen-check|gate|-|.pklith, hk.pklith.pkl, nix/pklith.nix|pklith gen --check|pklith gen|-|hk.pklith.pkl or nix/pklith.nix no longer matches .pklith; run pklith gen
pklith-check|gate|-|-|pklith check|-|-|a tracked file type has no row in .pklith, a row matches nothing, or a claimed check never reaches its files
# paradigm/V37, dev V3, V14: no committed file holds a name from the local,
# untracked .private/denylist, and none names a repository that
# dev/public-repos.toml does not list as PUBLIC: with or without a
# denylist, so CI, which has none, still keeps private names out.
name-guard|gate|-|**/*|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- name-guard {{files}}|-|-|a committed file holds a name from .private/denylist, or names a repository dev/public-repos.toml does not list
# paradigm/V15, dev V4: core.worktree in the shared .git/config redirects
# every worktree; the step refuses it.
no-core-worktree|gate|-|**/*|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- no-core-worktree|-|-|core.worktree is set in the shared .git/config; unset it
# dev V5: flake.lock holds one nixpkgs and one nixpkgs-lock node, so every
# input follows the fleet pin (paradigm/V20).
lock-graph|gate|-|flake.lock, flake.nix|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- lock-graph|-|-|flake.lock holds more than one nixpkgs or nixpkgs-lock node
# docs V1, dev T9: docs/PERFORMANCE.md is perf-doc's output for the
# baseline and the root C targets, never a hand edit. At commit: it
# reads 2 files and builds no bench, so a stale page never lands.
perf-doc|gate|-|benches/baseline.toml, docs/PERFORMANCE.md, SPEC.md|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- perf-doc --check|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- perf-doc|-|docs/PERFORMANCE.md is not perf-doc's output for benches/baseline.toml and SPEC.md; run cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- perf-doc
# Root T12, as lablith: this repository's GitHub workflows come from
# .actlith, rendered by the actlith in the dev shell; a hand edit, a stale
# render or an undeclared workflow file fails at commit.
actlith-gen-check|gate|-|.actlith, .github/workflows/**|actlith gen --check|actlith gen|-|a generated workflow no longer matches .actlith; run `actlith gen`
actlith-check|gate|-|.actlith, .github/workflows/**|actlith check|-|-|a workflow file is neither generated by .actlith nor listed hand-written
# dev T12: the crates.io tarball holds no SPEC.md and no .githooks/,
# holds every file building and licensing need, and every relative
# README link points at a file in it. `cargo package --list` builds
# nothing, so it runs at commit.
package-list|gate|-|Cargo.toml, README.md|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- package-list|-|-|cargo package -p chertmem --list ships a spec or hook, lacks a required file, or the README links to a file left out
# dev T11: the Rust crates block of THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is what
# Cargo.lock ships, never a hand edit. cargo tree and metadata run
# offline and need every crate's source, bpe's too, which no build
# downloads; `cargo fetch --locked` fills the registry first (a no-op,
# with no network, once it is full), and hk.pkl orders it after
# clippy. A failed cargo call is reported, not read as no crates.
notices|gate|-|Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md|cargo fetch --locked -q && cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- notices --check|cargo fetch --locked -q && cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- notices|-|THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md does not list the crates Cargo.lock ships; run cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- notices

# Offline, as in lablith: advisories need a fetched database, so they wait
# for the push and CI steps (root T12).
deny|supply|cargo-deny|Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, deny.toml|cargo deny check --disable-fetch licenses bans sources|-|-|a license, ban or source rule failed
# Every member, not only the root package: without --workspace the dev
# crate's examples never run.
doctest|test|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo test --workspace --doc -q|-|-|a doc example failed
rustdoc|lint|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items -q|-|RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings|docs do not build cleanly
test|coverage|cargo-nextest|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock|cargo nextest run --workspace --no-fail-fast --status-level fail --final-status-level fail|-|-|a test failed, or the suite is empty
# src/hook T12: the bpe build's own tests, the exact o200k count and the
# corpus check that the default estimate never undercounts it. Push
# only, alone (dev V10): it builds the root package with feature bpe.
test-bpe|coverage|cargo-nextest|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock|cargo nextest run -p chertmem --features bpe --no-fail-fast --status-level fail --final-status-level fail|-|-|a test of feature bpe failed: the exact count, or the default estimate undercounting it on the src/hook corpus
# dev V7: every Rust module with logic has a wired tests.rs mirror, ported
# from xenolith v0.1.0 to the dev crate.
rust-mirror|lint|-|**/*.rs|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- rust-mirror|-|-|a Rust file with logic has no sibling tests.rs wired by #[cfg(test)] mod tests;
# dev V8: a commit adding Rust code has a test commit before it in the
# push range, unless exempt in dev/tdd-order.exempt. Push only: the order
# is a property of history, and a RED commit must be committable.
tdd-order|coverage|-|**/*.rs, dev/tdd-order.exempt|cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- tdd-order|-|-|a commit adds Rust code with no test: commit before it in the push range
# paradigm/V25: line coverage floor, a ratchet; push only, alone (dev V10):
# cargo-llvm-cov builds the binaries too.
# Serial: cargo-llvm-cov runs plain cargo test, every test in 1 process,
# so ~10 parallel tests share one open-file limit (256 on macOS) and
# fail "unable to open database file"; nextest steps run 1 per process.
coverage|coverage|sherd|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, .coverage|sherd coverage --check|-|RUST_TEST_THREADS=1|line coverage fell below .coverage
# root V10, dev T2: the latency gate. Push only (category coverage), alone
# (dev V10): it builds and runs the release bench. Locally, not only in
# CI: the baseline's rows are this machine class's, and CI has none, so
# there it would hold without comparing. The 2 smallest stores keep the
# push near 40 s once the release build is cached, every store suite
# still measured; the larger ones run by hand before a re-record.
bench-gate|coverage|-|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, benches/baseline.toml|cargo bench -q -p chertmem --bench latency -- '/10?k-p52$' && cargo run -q -p chertmem-dev -- bench-gate 1k-p52 10k-p52|-|-|a bench median is over its baseline x (1 + tolerance) on this machine class; see docs/BENCHMARKS.md
# The crates.io tarball must build on its own: package-list checks the
# file list only, and missed vocab.bin (T14). Push only, alone: it
# compiles the packaged crate under target/package.
package-verify|coverage|-|**/*.rs, **/*.bin, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock|cargo package -q -p chertmem --locked --allow-dirty|-|-|the packaged crate failed to build (cargo package); one cause: a file it reads is missing from Cargo.toml include
## types
type|checks|min|exempt
*|trailing-whitespace, final-newline, line-endings, no-bom, no-merge-conflict, no-case-conflict, no-broken-symlinks, no-private-key, ripsecrets, typos, editorconfig-checker, no-local-paths, name-guard, no-core-worktree|-|-
editorconfig|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
gitattributes|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
md|markdownlint|-|-
nix|nixfmt, statix, deadnix|-|-
path:**/SPEC.md|markdownlint, mth-fmt, mth-check, sherd-check, sherd-nav, sherd-budget|-|-
path:.context-limits|sherd-budget|-|-
pklith|pklith-check, gen-check|-|-
pkl|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
pre-commit|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
pre-push|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
commit-msg|-|-|hook shim, same shape as the seeded ones; its steps live in hk.pkl
envrc|shellcheck|-|-
gitignore|-|-|git configuration; no linter reads ignore patterns
path:flake.lock|lock-graph|-|-
markdownlintignore|-|-|ignore patterns, no linter reads them
rs|rustfmt, clippy, rust-mirror, tdd-order, doctest, rustdoc, test, test-bpe, coverage, bench-gate, package-verify|-|-
toml|taplo|-|-
path:benches/baseline.toml|taplo, bench-gate, perf-doc|-|-
path:docs/PERFORMANCE.md|markdownlint, perf-doc|-|-
path:Cargo.lock|deny, notices, package-verify|-|-
path:THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md|markdownlint, notices|-|-
path:README.md|markdownlint, package-list|-|-
exempt|tdd-order|-|-
coverage|coverage|-|-
path:LICENSE|-|-|MIT license text, kept verbatim; the `*` checks still apply
yaml|yamllint|-|-
path:.actlith|actlith-gen-check, actlith-check|-|-
path:.github/workflows/*.yml|yamllint, actionlint, zizmor, actlith-gen-check, actlith-check|-|-
mjs|-|-|test-only oracle runner for src/grammar, never in the chert binary
txt|-|-|src/grammar corpus: input texts for the oracle and the grammar tests; tests/hook/corpus: the frozen README and docs the src/hook corpus reads (T14)
# src/hook T14 (R8): generated o200k subset, read by include_bytes!; the
# test-bpe drift test checks its bytes, package-verify that it ships.
bin|package-verify|-|-
compressed|-|-|golden output of cavemem compress, compared byte for byte by src/grammar tests
expanded|-|-|golden output of cavemem expand, compared byte for byte by src/grammar tests
path:tests/hook/fixtures/**/*.json|-|-|src/hook fixtures read by its tests: Claude Code 2.1.302 hook payloads recorded 2026-10-24 (src/hook R1)
